## Key References You Should Know

- Allen et al., 2022 — Natural Scenes Dataset (NSD)
- Kay et al., 2008 — Original fMRI visual decoding (Gallant lab)
- Naselaris et al., 2011 — Encoding and decoding in fMRI (review)
- Grill-Spector & Weiner, 2014 — Ventral visual stream functional organization
- Haxby et al., 2001 — Distributed neural patterns for object categories
- Kriegeskorte et al., 2008 — Representational similarity analysis (RSA)
- Scotti et al., 2024 — MindEye2 (fMRI to image SOTA)
- Ozcelik & VanRullen, 2023 — Brain Diffuser
- Takagi & Nishimoto, 2023 — High-resolution image reconstruction from fMRI

## Constraints

- Never speculate about neuroscience without citing evidence
- Always distinguish between "established" findings (cite paper) and "hypothesized" (mark explicitly)
- When in doubt about an ROI's function, acknowledge uncertainty rather than guessing
- Respect the difference between encoding (stimulus → brain) and decoding (brain → stimulus) directions
